---
import Divider from "../../../components/ui/Divider.astro";
import Layout from "../../../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout>
  <div class="container my-4">
    <div class="row justify-content-center">
      <div class="col-sm-12 col-md-10">
        <a
          href="/courses/eng-design-fab/"
          class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-light mb-3"
        >
          <i class="si-arrow-left"></i> Back
        </a>

        <h1>Session 27: Reflect &amp; Defend</h1>
        <p class="text-sn-theme">Racquet Ball Launcher Project &mdash; Milestone 6 of 6</p>
        <Divider variant="8" classes="mb-5" />

        <!-- Launch / Concept -->
        <section id="launch">
          <h2>Closing the Loop</h2>
          <p>
            This is where the project closes the loop &mdash; the Reflect
            stage of Session 1's design cycle, run for real, at full scale,
            over an entire quarter.
          </p>

          <p>
            A team that missed targets on Field Test Day but can clearly
            diagnose why demonstrates the same competency as a team that hit
            all three. Misses are valuable material here, not something to
            minimize.
          </p>

          <p>
            A team that hit all three targets doesn't get to skip real
            reflection either &mdash; your model's actual limitations are
            still worth surfacing, win or lose.
          </p>
        </section>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="my-5" />

        <!-- Build -->
        <section id="build">
          <h2>Build</h2>

          <p>
            Prepare a short presentation or written defense &mdash; check
            with your instructor which format &mdash; covering all four of
            these:
          </p>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>1. Your Independent Variable</h3>
          <p>
            Which one you chose, and why &mdash; reference your actual
            Session 15&ndash;16 reasoning, not a retroactive justification
            that sounds better now.
          </p>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>2. What Your Data Showed</h3>
          <p>
            Summarize your calibration model from Sessions 21&ndash;23, and
            how it changed after Sessions 24&ndash;25's iteration.
          </p>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>3. Your Field Test Day Performance</h3>
          <p>
            State your results honestly, misses included. For any miss,
            give a specific diagnosis &mdash; a model limitation at the edge
            of your usable range, field conditions, inconsistent execution
            &mdash; not a vague "we were off."
          </p>

          <hr class="my-4" />

          <h3>4. Your Notebook's Evolution</h3>
          <p>
            Submit your full notebook, showing the model's evolution from
            your first Session 15&ndash;16 entry through today &mdash; not
            just a polished final summary.
          </p>
        </section>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="my-5" />

        <!-- Checkpoint -->
        <section id="checkpoint">
          <h2>Checkpoint</h2>

          <p>Before you present or submit, confirm:</p>

          <ul>
            <li>Your IV explanation references your actual original reasoning, not a rewritten version</li>
            <li>Every miss (if any) has a specific, named cause &mdash; not a vague explanation</li>
            <li>Your notebook is complete from Sessions 15&ndash;16 through today, not just a final-state summary</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="my-5" />

        <!-- Reflection -->
        <section id="reflection">
          <h2>Reflection</h2>

          <p>Answer these on your own. Reflections are individual, even when the rest of the session was team work.</p>

          <ol>
            <li>If you ran this entire project again from Session 15, what's the one thing you'd do differently, knowing what you know now?</li>
            <li>Next quarter you'll design and build an arcade cabinet for a real client, on a CNC router. Which habit from this project do you most want to carry into it &mdash; and which one do you most need to leave behind?</li>
          </ol>
        </section>

        <Divider variant="8" classes="my-5" />

        <!-- Submit -->
        <section id="submit">
          <h2>Submit</h2>

          <p>
            Submit your presentation or written defense, and your complete
            design notebook.
          </p>

          <h1
            class="text-center mt-5 text-sn-theme border border-primary slow-flash"
          >
            Project Complete
          </h1>
        </section>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
